    "q-111446": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111446",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the real solution to the equation ${x}^{3}=-512.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can solve this equation by taking the $3$rd root of each side and solving for $x.$ Since $n=3$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =-512 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}} & =\\sqrt[3]{-512} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[3]{(-8)^{3}} \\\\ x & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-8.$",
