    "q-111455": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111455",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the real solution to the equation $3(x+7)^{9}=1\\,536.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can solve this equation by isolating the $(x+7)^{9}$ term and then taking the $9$th root of each side.\n\nFirst, let's isolate the $(x+7)^{9}$ term on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+7)^{9} & =1\\,536 \\\\ (x+7)^{9} & =512\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the $9$th root of each side and solve for $x.$ Since $n=9$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+7)^{9} & =512 \\\\ \\sqrt[9]{(x+7)^{9}} & =\\sqrt[9]{512} \\\\ x+7 & =\\sqrt[9]{{2}^{9}} \\\\ x+7 & =2 \\\\ x & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
