    "q-111453": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111453",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the real solution to the equation $(x-5)^{3}=-27.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can solve this equation by taking the $3$rd root of each side and solving for $x.$\nSince $n=3$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-5)^{3} & =-27 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(x-5)^{3}} & =\\sqrt[3]{-27} \\\\ x-5 & =\\sqrt[3]{(-3)^{3}} \\\\ x-5 & =-3 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
